WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.348 --> 00:00:04.818
(slow nonchalant music)

00:00:04.818 --> 00:00:06.683
- Do you think you can be sexy

00:00:06.683 --> 00:00:09.175
and have diarrhea at the same time?

00:00:09.781 --> 00:00:12.503
- Not while you're
having the diarrhea, no.

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:19.420
- I'm here today with Dr.
Deleve, who is a poop expert,

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.785
also known as a gastroenterologist, right?

00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:23.662
- Yes

00:00:23.662 --> 00:00:25.230
- Okay, and what does that mean exactly?

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.755
- That's a doctor who takes care of people

00:00:26.755 --> 00:00:28.176
who have problems with their swallowing,

00:00:28.176 --> 00:00:30.057
their stomach, or their guts.

00:00:30.057 --> 00:00:31.687
- Okay, so you see a lot of poop.

00:00:31.687 --> 00:00:32.502
- See a lot of poop.

00:00:32.502 --> 00:00:35.866
- I asked my coworkers to send
me pictures of their poop.

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:37.559
And they did and it was so gross

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:39.084
that I could not show them to you.

00:00:39.084 --> 00:00:40.354
(laughing)

00:00:40.354 --> 00:00:43.668
I questioned my sanity,
looking at my coworkers' poops.

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:46.051
Then what I had them do is describe them

00:00:46.051 --> 00:00:49.911
to an artist who made
some artist-renderings.

00:00:49.911 --> 00:00:51.923
I was wondering if you
could grade the poops.

00:00:51.923 --> 00:00:52.564
- Absolutely.

00:00:52.564 --> 00:00:53.783
- Here we have this one.

00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:54.890
- Yeah, those are little pebble-like

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.541
stools and the reason they're like that

00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:58.965
is because the poop is taking
too long to get through

00:00:58.965 --> 00:01:00.511
the gut so it's getting dried out.

00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:01.932
That's a sign of constipation.

00:01:01.932 --> 00:01:05.330
- That's one person who
I guess was constipated.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:10.111
- This is a poop that's not the ideal poop

00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:11.636
but it's still within the normal range.

00:01:11.636 --> 00:01:12.973
It's slightly constipated,

00:01:12.973 --> 00:01:15.221
it's rocks kind of
congregated into a sausage

00:01:15.221 --> 00:01:18.083
and that's a little more
on the constipated side

00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:20.194
than a smooth sausage would be.

00:01:20.194 --> 00:01:21.427
Ah, the perfect sausage.

00:01:21.427 --> 00:01:22.772
That's a log.

00:01:22.772 --> 00:01:25.486
If you want a stool that
looks like the ideal poop,

00:01:25.486 --> 00:01:26.669
this is the ideal poop.

00:01:26.669 --> 00:01:28.780
- This is it, whoever gave me this one,

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.252
I think it was you (bleep),
you got the perfect poop.

00:01:33.252 --> 00:01:33.920
- That's a green poop.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:34.673
- [Voiceover] So green is okay?

00:01:34.673 --> 00:01:35.905
- [Voiceover] Green is a perfect poop.

00:01:35.905 --> 00:01:36.950
- Yeah?

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.518
- Normal is brown, green, or yellow.

00:01:38.518 --> 00:01:39.333
That's all normal.

00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:40.419
- We got this one.

00:01:40.419 --> 00:01:42.874
- That's a mushier stool,
that looks like it's heading

00:01:42.874 --> 00:01:44.599
towards diarrhea when you're getting these

00:01:44.599 --> 00:01:47.294
little flakes that are kind
of watery at the edges.

00:01:47.294 --> 00:01:49.677
That suggests that you're developing

00:01:49.677 --> 00:01:52.519
a looser stool if that's
not your normal pattern.

00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:54.295
Then you have to wonder
about dietary things

00:01:54.295 --> 00:01:56.405
you might be ingesting like lactose,

00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:57.722
if you're lactose-intolerant,

00:01:57.722 --> 00:01:59.979
or fructose, if you're
fructose-intolerant.

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:00.877
- Too many dried fruits?

00:02:00.877 --> 00:02:04.556
- Too many dried fruits,
too much fruit juice.

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:06.480
- Alright, so...

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.206
- That's a very nicely shaped
log with some corn in it.

00:02:09.206 --> 00:02:10.188
That's perfectly normal.

00:02:10.188 --> 00:02:12.695
- Why do we see it, why does
it just come out as corn?

00:02:12.695 --> 00:02:14.518
- It's not well digested.

00:02:14.518 --> 00:02:16.269
It travels through you and
that's probably a good thing,

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:18.228
it means your transit time from mouth

00:02:18.228 --> 00:02:19.880
to the toilet bowl is fast.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:20.737
- This is (bleep).

00:02:20.737 --> 00:02:22.764
- I've not really seen a
Mt. Everest-looking stool

00:02:22.764 --> 00:02:24.812
but it looks to me like
this came out more like

00:02:24.812 --> 00:02:26.901
toothpaste and again it's a softer stool.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:29.493
Some people have one loose stool a day.

00:02:29.493 --> 00:02:32.160
If that's your normal
pattern, that can be okay.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:33.989
- How do you know when you're

00:02:33.989 --> 00:02:35.511
having a poop that's problematic?

00:02:35.511 --> 00:02:38.060
- You probably should see a doctor if

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.983
what you're normally
doing suddenly changes.

00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:41.717
You should see a doctor if your stools

00:02:41.717 --> 00:02:43.222
are suddenly coming out pencil-thin.

00:02:43.222 --> 00:02:44.977
Consistently, not one day,

00:02:44.977 --> 00:02:47.648
but consistently coming out really thin.

00:02:47.648 --> 00:02:49.533
If it's coming out
really funny colors like

00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:51.685
pitch-black or bloody or white.

00:02:51.685 --> 00:02:53.211
- I'm not afraid to talk about poop,

00:02:53.211 --> 00:02:55.488
you certainly are not
afraid to talk about poop,

00:02:55.488 --> 00:02:57.307
it's your career.

00:02:57.307 --> 00:02:59.187
Why do you think people are so

00:02:59.187 --> 00:03:01.292
uncomfortable discussing this?

00:03:01.292 --> 00:03:02.761
- It's a mystery to me why people are

00:03:02.761 --> 00:03:06.000
as jittery about talking
about poop as they are.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.122
I think it's because it
stinks and people just don't

00:03:08.122 --> 00:03:10.805
like talking about bodily
functions that stink.

